title: "The European Cycling Risk Index: Methodology, Validation, and a City-Level Analysis of 219 Cities"
authors:
  - family-names: Rotariu
    given-names: Victor
    affiliation: Defensive Pedal Research
type: report
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-15
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://victorwho.github.io/european-cycling-risk-ranking/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/victorwho/european-cycling-risk-ranking"
keywords:
  - cycling safety
  - road safety
  - urban cycling
  - risk modelling
  - city ranking
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Europe
abstract: >-
  219 European cities across 30 countries ranked on the cycling risk of their
  street networks, using a production per-road risk model validated against
  3.98 billion measured bicycle passages and 1,169 serious injuries. Three
  dimensions (street-network risk, journey risk, low-stress accessibility),
  90% rank intervals from 2,000 method respecifications, per-city profiles,
  and an open data supplement.
